2,"Nahuatl, Eastern Huasteca",https://accentnetwork.com/nahuatl-eastern-huasteca/,"April 22, 2025 - Eastern Huasteca Nahuatl includes glottalized sounds and complex vowels, challenging for outsiders. Primarily follows VSO, with tone marking grammatical distinctions. Text expands by around 10%, impacting subtitle alignment. Respectful terms and cultural expressions may lack direct translations. Compatibility with fonts supporting diacritics is essential on digital platforms. Eastern Huasteca traditions are rich in stories, music, and community events.","Nahuatl, Eastern Huasteca",Uto-Aztecan
